2. How to get the source
------------------------

The complete corresponding source of the WebAssembly files in this release is in the directory "source/" of
the release directory (the same place that serves the WebAssembly files), as runtime-source-<version>.tar.gz,
with SHA256SUMS. It contains the source tree of Icarus Verilog, the patches, the build scripts, the records named in this NOTICE and in README.md, this NOTICE and LICENSES/. The same source is also in the repository cresmaia/verilog-web-runtime.
How the WebAssembly files are built from it: README.md in the source (section "Reproducing the build") and
build/eta2-check-scripts/ (copies of the scripts that made them; the paths of the machine where they ran are replaced, see build/README.md).
The circuit diagram parts (sections 3.6 and 3.7) are not built from that tree. The sources of elkjs, of the Eclipse Layout Kernel, of the Eclipse Modeling Framework classes
and of the Xtext library (org.eclipse.xtext.xbase.lib) classes inside elkjs are in the directory "source/third-party/" of the release directory, with their sha256 in SHA256SUMS; section 3.7 says which file is the source of which part.

